<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Malta</h1><p class="st-meta">1964 CE – present · capital Valletta</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Mediterranean island republic, independent from Britain since 1964, a republic since 1974, and a member of the EU since 2004 and the eurozone since 2008.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Malta gained independence as the State of Malta on 21 September 1964, having been a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/crown-colony-of-malta">Crown Colony of Malta</a> under British rule since the early 19th century. Under the 1964 constitution <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-ii">Elizabeth II</a> remained queen of Malta, with a governor-general exercising executive authority on her behalf.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After the Malta Labour Party under Dom Mintoff won the 1971 elections, Malta declared itself a republic within the Commonwealth on 13 December 1974. A defence agreement with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> expired on 31 March 1979, Freedom Day, and the British base closed. Malta adopted a policy of neutrality in 1980 and joined the Non-Aligned Movement. In 1989 it hosted a summit between George H. W. Bush and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a>. Politics since 1966 has been dominated by the Labour Party and the Nationalist Party in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliamentary-democracy">parliamentary system</a> modelled on Westminster.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>A referendum on 8 March 2003 backed joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>, with 53.65 percent in favour, and Malta joined on 1 May 2004 and the eurozone on 1 January 2008. The Labour Party has governed since 2013, and Robert Abela has been prime minister since 13 January 2020. Myriam Spiteri Debono was elected president by Parliament on 27 March 2024.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/malta.jpg" alt="Malta" width="330" height="220"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Malta.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1964 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Valletta</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dom Mintoff, Robert Abela</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Maltese, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/malta">Malta</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Malta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1995&amp;focus=malta" aria-label="Malta on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: where Malta lay"><image href="/maps/globes/g000n30.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5995 4433L5995 4433"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5995 4433h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5995 4433h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5995 4433h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Valletta. <a href="/atlas?year=1995&amp;focus=malta">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
